WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:09.260
Did you know that, every second, you are
experiencing microwave radiation from

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:15.349
space? Yes, that's right: microwaves. The same radiation heating your leftovers is

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:20.029
what's heating the universe. The first
time humans saw this cosmic radiation

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:24.830
was while channel surfing on our first
television sets. We didn't know it then,

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:30.140
but we were watching the oldest
radiation. Within this radiation is our

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.840
history, it describes the conditions of the early

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:39.559
universe and today is the strongest
evidence for a Hot Big Bang model. Let's

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:45.559
slow down--to understand how all this
works, we need to travel back in time one

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:53.420
month after the beginning of the cosmos,
13.8 billion years ago. Less than a

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.860
second after the hot big bang, the
universe underwent a period of massive

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:03.260
inflation. During this period of
inflation, everything grew by 60-e

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.240
foldings. After this short-lived
inflation epoch, the universe has

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.640
continued to expand, and has become a
dense soup of particles about a billion

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:19.700
degrees Celsius. That's roughly a million
times hotter than the sun today- so hot

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.830
that matter and energy are essentially
the same thing. Our universe soup is

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:31.220
called the photon-baryon fluid because
it's made of mostly photons and baryons

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:37.310
with a dash of electrons. Photons are the
light particles which carry the energy

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.920
of radiation. They travel in the form of
waves: short wavelengths carry high

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.369
energy, long wavelengths carry less
energy.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.079
When a photon is radiated away, it
retains information about the source

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:58.380
such as its temperature, direction, and
even its chemical composition. They carry

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.549
this information until they interact
with matter, which means that the photons

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:09.000
we detect today provide us with the
history of their origins. Baryons include

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.090
protons and neutrons which make up the
nucleus of the ATOM. The atom is the

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.450
fundamental building block for all
matter. The simplest atom, Hydrogen,

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:26.340
requires one electron orbiting a single
proton. But because the cosmos is so

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:32.370
small and hot, the photons are energetic
enough to blast electrons out of orbit--

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:39.209
thus no atoms are formed and nothing
"matters". The universe pretty much stays

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:46.530
as this hot cosmic soup for a while, so
let's fast forward. It is now 380,000

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.920
years later. As the universe expands, it
stretches the wavelength of photons

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.359
resulting in a distribution of energy
across space. The dispersion of this

00:02:57.359 --> 00:03:04.049
energy has caused the cosmic soup to cool to about 3000 degrees Celsius, roughly

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:09.569
half the temperature of the sun today.
Since the photons are traveling with

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.019
longer wavelengths they are not
energetic enough to scatter off

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:18.540
electrons in orbit. The photon-baryon
fluid has evaporated. Let there be light...

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:26.220
and matter. This instant is recognized as
the surface of last scattering, the first

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:33.599
light of the cosmos. A snapshot of the
young universe. Photons can now move much

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:38.060
longer distances and carry the
information about this time further.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:43.079
Electrons are free to orbit baryonic
nuclei forming the basic blocks of all

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:48.470
life. As we move forward in time, the
photon wavelength continues to stretch.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:55.769
At 100 million years, matter condenses to
form stars. At 600 million years, our home

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:06.780
galaxy. The Milky Way is born. At 8.6 billion years, the sun forms, giving birth to
our solar system.  Today the universe is

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:13.840
13.8 billion years old. It has continued
to expand and the photons of the early

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.000
cosmos have continued to stretch,
becoming invisible low-energy microwaves,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:27.160
which are nearly radio waves. In the year
1964 (modern time), two scientists at Bell Labs detect

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:32.140
this radiation as noise in their Radio
Telescope. After cleaning up the "white

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:37.900
dielectric material"-- bird poop-- they think
is interfering with their data, they

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.990
discover this cosmic radiation is
constant from every direction in the sky.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:48.580
After a paper publication, this apparent
noise from the sky is recognized as

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.500
remnant radiation from the earliest
observable moment in the evolution of

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.060
the universe, a baby picture of the
cosmos, called

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:04.060
the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB). This radiation from the CMB is what heats the

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:10.390
empty voids of space to 3 degrees
above absolute zero. 2.725 Kelvin.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:18.070
Today we know the CMB is the
heat radiation from the evaporation of

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:23.350
the early cosmic soup, it is evidence
that the universe was once a hot dense

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:27.550
fluid that has been expanding. We
interpret this as evidence of the

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:32.860
big bang, but we don't know what happened before this picture.  Cosmologists

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.530
consider a number of origins for the
cosmos

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:40.960
based on this CMB radiation. But the most widely accepted model is the Hot Big Bang.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.820
If the universe weren't expanding,
we wouldn't be here and it would still

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:50.160
be a hot soup of energy and matter.

00:05:56.729 --> 00:05:58.789
 

